tNokia 刚刚崩溃了 IIoT 堆栈</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/industrial-edge-ai-networking-why-rajantnokia-just-collapsed-the-iiot-stack</link><description>工业边缘人工智能网络：Rajant-Nokia 将网状网络和边缘人工智能合并到一个堆栈中。更少的供应商、更快的部署、更高的锁定。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/industrial-edge-ai-networking-why-rajantnokia-just-collapsed-the-iiot-stack.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:40:06 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/industrial-edge-ai-networking-why-rajantnokia-just-collapsed-the-iiot-stack</guid></item><item><title>发现揭示了太空中复杂芳香分子的快速途径</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/discovery-reveals-rapid-pathways-to-complex-aromatic-molecules-in-space</link><description>由夏威夷大学马诺阿化学系领导的一个研究小组发现了一种在太空中更快形成大型碳基分子的方法，有助于解决有关宇宙的一些组成部分如何生长的长期谜团。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/discovery-reveals-rapid-pathways-to-complex-aromatic-molecules-in-space.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:25:06 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/discovery-reveals-rapid-pathways-to-complex-aromatic-molecules-in-space</guid></item><item><title>新线索表明破坏性免疫细胞如何对大脑造成严重破坏</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/new-clues-suggest-how-destructive-immune-cells-wreak-havoc-in-the-brain</link><description>几年前，科学家在死于阿尔茨海默病的人的脑组织中发现了一些令人惊讶的东西：白细胞会因应对外来威胁而繁殖，而在健康的大脑中很少见。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/new-clues-suggest-how-destructive-immune-cells-wreak-havoc-in-the-brain2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:10:06 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/new-clues-suggest-how-destructive-immune-cells-wreak-havoc-in-the-brain</guid></item><item><title>在地球上制造天王星和海王星冰</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/making-uranian-and-neptunian-ice-on-earth</link><description>研究人员在金刚石砧之间压碎并加热冰，以确认冰巨星温暖地幔中可能存在的冰相的存在。&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/making-uranian-and-neptunian-ice-on-earth.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:55:06 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/making-uranian-and-neptunian-ice-on-earth</guid></item><item><title>新的脉冲序列方法旨在提高量子控制的精度</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/new-pulse-train-method-aims-to-improve-precision-in-quantum-control</link><description>量子技术有望通过操纵原子和分子的能量状态来改变从医学和传感到计算和通信等领域。这些操纵是通过用激光脉冲控制量子态来实现的。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/new-pulse-train-method-aims-to-improve-precision-in-quantum-control.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:40:06 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/new-pulse-train-method-aims-to-improve-precision-in-quantum-control</guid></item><item><title>人工智能很快就能通过神经反馈感知“这不是我的意思”来推断人类意图</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/ai-could-soon-infer-human-intent-by-sensing-thats-not-what-i-meant-through-neural-feedback</link><description>人工智能能够从大脑信号中识别出一个人无声的“这不是我的意思”反应并自行调整其行为的未来已经越来越近了。韩国科学技术院的研究人员开发了一种技术，可以通过脑电波检测人类和人工智能之间的认知不匹配，使人工智能系统能够根据人类的目标实时修改其行为。这一成就预计将加速从遵循明确命令的人工智能向能够推断人类意图的人工智能的转变。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/ai-could-soon-infer-human-intent-by-sensing-thats-not-what-i-meant-through-neural-feedback2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:25:06 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/ai-could-soon-infer-human-intent-by-sensing-thats-not-what-i-meant-through-neural-feedback</guid></item><item><title>科学家可视化蛋白质隐藏的水结构，这可能有助于定义生物功能</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/scientists-visualize-proteins-hidden-water-architecture-that-may-help-define-biological-function</link><description>几十年来，科学家主要通过两个定义特征来了解蛋白质：氨基酸序列和三维结构。该框架推动了生物学、生物技术和医学领域的重大进步，最终催生了能够以极高的准确性预测蛋白质结构的人工智能工具。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/scientists-visualize-proteins-hidden-water-architecture-that-may-help-define-biological-function.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:10:06 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/09/scientists-visualize-proteins-hidden-water-architecture-that-may-help-define-biological-function</guid></item></channel></rss>